            <div xml:id="d40">

                <pb facs="0062" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg52"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50/3827: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-24T18:00:00-04:00">June 24, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4984. We assume from your 4782, June 15, 5 p.m. and previous telegrams that the
                    “deadlock” referred to is that in London between the civil servants and the
                    Ministers.</p>
                <p>We would be keenly interested in any further information you can give us on this
                    matter, particularly concerning thought on the ministerial level, and any
                    suggestions you may have as to how progress may be expedited.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
